\subsection{Pipeline Synchronization Logic}

The hardware pipeline is synchronized using a deterministic jitter clock
that prevents timing-based inference attacks. Each stage commits its
state using a sealed register block:

\begin{equation}
    \Sigma_{i+1} = H(\Sigma_i \parallel \Delta_i) \pmod q
\end{equation}

where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\Sigma_i$ is the sealed state of stage $i$,
    \item $\Delta_i$ is the encrypted-domain output of stage $i$,
    \item $H$ is a cryptographic hash function bound to the silicon identity.
\end{itemize}

This ensures that pipeline transitions cannot be replayed or forged.

\subsection{Encrypted Bus Protocol}

All inter-module communication uses ciphertext-only routing:

\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{T}(c) = c \oplus \eta \pmod q
\end{equation}

where $\eta$ is a randomized bus noise mask refreshed every 32 cycles.

This prevents electromagnetic or timing-based extraction of ciphertext structure.